It is distributed as binaries that statically link third-party Rust crates and
embed a built web bundle, so the licenses of both travel with every release.
The full resolved inventory is in licenses/THIRD-PARTY.md, regenerated from the
lockfiles by `make licenses`. What follows is only what places an obligation
beyond including a copyright notice and a permission notice.

Build-time tooling is deliberately absent from that inventory. Most of this
project's npm dependency count is Vite, Playwright, Expo and Metro, none of
which is distributed, so their licenses place no obligation on the binaries.
What ships from the npm side is nine packages.

